1
00:00:26,460 --> 00:00:28,400
Einar...

2
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:52,350
No, wait. Wait!

3
00:00:52,350 --> 00:00:53,600
Wait!

4
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:18,440
Damn it...

5
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:23,040
Why am I here?

6
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:29,680
I mustn't fall.

7
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:33,010
If I fall down there...

8
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:45,440
No! Please, don't!

9
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:48,800
I'm begging you!

10
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:08,880
Good morning, Thorfinn.

11
00:02:09,270 --> 00:02:12,590
You were screaming even more
than usual this morning.

12
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:21,600
I dreamed about falling down a cliff.

13
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:25,720
You remember your dream this morning?

14
00:02:26,290 --> 00:02:27,850
A little.

15
00:02:27,850 --> 00:02:31,270
You were saying all kinds
of things in your sleep,

16
00:02:31,270 --> 00:02:35,490
like "Father" and "Askeladd."

17
00:02:36,070 --> 00:02:39,120
Is "Askeladd" someone's name?

18
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:23,320
No matter what...

19
00:04:25,020 --> 00:04:31,810
An Empty Man

20
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:29,350
No matter what I do,
I can't fully remember my dreams.

21
00:04:33,490 --> 00:04:38,470
I followed her wondering what she wanted
to show me, and it was a moth this big!

22
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:37,060
I know only that they're horrifying.

23
00:04:38,470 --> 00:04:43,510
I spent a half-hour explaining to
Lotta that it was a moth, not a butterfly

24
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:42,020
And I feel like...

25
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:47,910
I feel like I've forgotten
something really important.

26
00:04:43,510 --> 00:04:46,150
but she insisted on keeping it.

27
00:04:46,150 --> 00:04:49,550
Then Mom suddenly showed up, and...

28
00:04:52,060 --> 00:04:55,960
It's like a fish bone stuck in my throat.

29
00:04:57,760 --> 00:05:00,800
It scares me. I wish I could truly forget.

30
00:05:02,220 --> 00:05:04,920
But I get the sense it's something
I mustn't forget.

31
00:05:10,460 --> 00:05:11,680
I wonder what it is...

32
00:05:26,740 --> 00:05:28,180
Pull!

33
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:34,080
Hey, look at how much
their wheat has grown already.

34
00:05:34,810 --> 00:05:37,820
Maybe the land's fertile
because they just cleared it.

35
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:40,770
No, it's Einar.

36
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:44,720
They suddenly made a bunch of progress
clearing the land since he showed up.

37
00:05:45,550 --> 00:05:47,850
Push!

38
00:05:55,380 --> 00:05:57,980
The master's out of his mind.

39
00:05:57,980 --> 00:06:04,650
Farm work is for free men,
and he's allowing slaves to do it.

40
00:06:05,610 --> 00:06:10,870
This isn't right, even if it's on his orders.

41
00:06:10,870 --> 00:06:17,270
The world will fall into chaos if slaves
are treated the same as retainers.

42
00:06:17,270 --> 00:06:18,880
Right, guys?

43
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:32,540
Askeladd is the man who killed my father.

44
00:06:35,310 --> 00:06:37,800
He was a Danish warmonger.

45
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:43,050
He was a strong and cruel man.

46
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:46,230
Catch.

47
00:06:46,230 --> 00:06:47,660
Oh, right.

48
00:06:49,320 --> 00:06:52,790
So, he showed up in your dream?

49
00:06:53,150 --> 00:06:55,160
I'm not sure.

50
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:03,100
I followed Askeladd onto the battlefield,

51
00:07:04,630 --> 00:07:07,080
so I could avenge my father.

52
00:07:07,930 --> 00:07:12,980
I fought for ten—no, 11 years.

53
00:07:15,920 --> 00:07:17,620
I hated him so much.

54
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:20,530
I wanted to kill him.

55
00:07:24,670 --> 00:07:27,570
So, did you get revenge?

56
00:07:30,010 --> 00:07:31,330
No.

57
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:39,660
Askeladd was killed by another man
right before my eyes.

58
00:07:44,390 --> 00:07:46,700
Thorfinn, throw me the next one.

59
00:07:47,180 --> 00:07:48,650
Oh, right.

60
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:53,100
Hup.

61
00:07:55,290 --> 00:07:59,590
Well, I don't know the details,

62
00:07:59,590 --> 00:08:04,060
but I'm starting to understand
why you're always so listless.

63
00:08:07,090 --> 00:08:12,540
If you're dreaming about him,
then you must not be over it yet.

64
00:08:13,540 --> 00:08:20,180
You're right. Maybe you're right, but...

65
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:26,340
That's not all. There's something else.

66
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:31,140
I feel like I've forgotten
something more important.

67
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:35,340
Something very important.

68
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:50,480
Well, it's not the kind of thing you can
get over just because someone tells you to.

69
00:08:52,900 --> 00:08:58,980
But your quest for revenge is over now.

70
00:09:00,590 --> 00:09:05,630
And besides, hating a dead man
won't get you anywhere.

71
00:09:06,130 --> 00:09:07,000
Isn't that right?

72
00:09:10,850 --> 00:09:12,550
Stay back, Thorfinn!

73
00:09:12,550 --> 00:09:19,260
Become a true warrior, son of Thors...

74
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:25,540
I don't hate him anymore,

75
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:30,640
which is exactly my problem.

76
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:37,740
Without my hate,

77
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:42,200
I'm empty.

78
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:50,180
I survived on my hatred alone.

79
00:09:53,760 --> 00:09:57,500
I don't know anything
besides the battlefield.

80
00:09:59,350 --> 00:10:01,860
I don't know the first thing
about fixing a roof.

81
00:10:02,620 --> 00:10:03,980
I can't do anything.

82
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:07,140
I don't even know what I should be doing.

83
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:11,820
I'm empty.

84
00:10:16,530 --> 00:10:18,290
Work.

85
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:20,110
Sir!

86
00:10:20,110 --> 00:10:23,540
If you've got time to flap
your gums, then work.

87
00:10:23,540 --> 00:10:26,980
That's not the only job
I've got for you today.

88
00:10:37,990 --> 00:10:40,800
You ready? Watch this.

89
00:10:56,920 --> 00:10:58,260
Give it a try.

90
00:10:58,820 --> 00:11:00,960
Catch some big, fleshy ones.

91
00:11:05,370 --> 00:11:08,590
Huh? It's not spreading.

92
00:11:08,590 --> 00:11:10,130
Pull yourself together.

93
00:11:10,130 --> 00:11:14,490
We can't eat meat right now
because it's Lent.

94
00:11:14,490 --> 00:11:17,640
Are you trying to force this old man
to eat nothing but wheat?

95
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:23,730
Hey, looking good.

96
00:11:24,210 --> 00:11:27,050
It's no use. I didn't catch a single one.

97
00:11:27,050 --> 00:11:31,860
Put more spin on it, like this.

98
00:11:31,860 --> 00:11:35,170
Don't keep throwing in the same area.

99
00:11:35,170 --> 00:11:36,180
Okay.

100
00:11:42,740 --> 00:11:47,560
You can start learning things one at a time.

101
00:11:51,130 --> 00:11:54,650
If you're empty, then you can
fit anything inside you.

102
00:11:54,650 --> 00:12:00,020
In fact, it's better to be empty
if you want to be reborn.

103
00:12:01,050 --> 00:12:03,190
What? Were you eavesdropping?

104
00:12:03,190 --> 00:12:04,430
I just happened to overhear.

105
00:12:10,260 --> 00:12:13,500
Can I be reborn?

106
00:12:14,690 --> 00:12:18,200
Work. Your hands aren't moving.

107
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:27,370
It's so cold.

108
00:12:27,370 --> 00:12:29,420
It's definitely gonna snow.

109
00:12:29,420 --> 00:12:32,840
Catching fish will be rough in this cold.

110
00:12:33,260 --> 00:12:36,500
I'd like to redeem myself, though.

111
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:39,760
Yesterday, between the two of us,

112
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:42,930
all we caught were three little fish
and a bunch of clams.

113
00:12:43,430 --> 00:12:45,180
Right, Thorfinn?

114
00:12:45,610 --> 00:12:50,180
Huh? Oh, sorry. I wasn't listening.

115
00:12:50,690 --> 00:12:53,820
Were you lost in thought again?

116
00:12:56,960 --> 00:13:00,090
Do you think people can change?

117
00:13:01,560 --> 00:13:03,360
What does it take for someone to change?

118
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:11,530
Thorfinn, you used to be a warrior, right?

119
00:13:11,530 --> 00:13:13,730
Huh? Yeah.

120
00:13:13,730 --> 00:13:16,340
Warriors are, you know...

121
00:13:16,340 --> 00:13:21,340
"Life's all about carrying axes into battle,
plundering the spoils, and drinking beer!"

122
00:13:21,340 --> 00:13:23,350
"Hardy har har!"

123
00:13:23,350 --> 00:13:24,580
Those guys, right?

124
00:13:25,970 --> 00:13:32,100
M-More or less. I didn't carry an axe, though.

125
00:13:34,360 --> 00:13:40,380
Looking at you now, there isn't anyone
who'd think you're a former warrior.

126
00:13:43,190 --> 00:13:44,630
You think so?

127
00:13:44,630 --> 00:13:47,240
"You think so?"

128
00:13:47,610 --> 00:13:51,900
Take a look at your own face in the water.

129
00:13:56,780 --> 00:14:02,630
I'm really glad I didn't meet you
back when you were still a warrior.

130
00:14:03,540 --> 00:14:07,420
Worst case, you might've killed me.

131
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:12,940
People can change, Thorfinn.

132
00:14:13,800 --> 00:14:18,660
You're probably on your way to
becoming a better person right now.

133
00:14:30,720 --> 00:14:33,080
You think so?

134
00:14:34,460 --> 00:14:35,580
I do.

135
00:14:39,550 --> 00:14:41,960
Thank you, Einar.

136
00:14:47,140 --> 00:14:49,680
What's wrong? Einar—

137
00:15:02,950 --> 00:15:04,000
The wheat...

138
00:15:31,420 --> 00:15:32,540
It's all...

139
00:15:34,350 --> 00:15:38,780
Did people do this? Why?

140
00:15:41,660 --> 00:15:44,320
Wheat is a hardy crop.

141
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:51,440
It gets back up on its own
even if the wind blows it down.

142
00:15:52,850 --> 00:15:55,460
They knew exactly what they were doing.

143
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:58,640
They dug up the roots.

144
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:06,510
Hey, where are you going?

145
00:16:06,510 --> 00:16:08,000
It was the retainers.

146
00:16:08,550 --> 00:16:11,510
They're the only ones who would've done this.

147
00:16:11,510 --> 00:16:14,050
Wait. What are you planning to do?

148
00:16:14,050 --> 00:16:15,000
Einar...

149
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:17,210
Don't you get it?

150
00:16:17,210 --> 00:16:19,520
If slaves attack free men...

151
00:16:20,030 --> 00:16:23,180
I don't care. I'll kill them.

152
00:16:23,900 --> 00:16:25,310
Calm down.

153
00:16:25,310 --> 00:16:27,930
We don't have proof they did it.

154
00:16:27,930 --> 00:16:30,530
Even if we question them,
they're bound to deny it.

155
00:16:30,530 --> 00:16:32,150
Stop, Einar.

156
00:16:32,150 --> 00:16:35,040
Let's talk to Pater first.

157
00:16:36,990 --> 00:16:38,740
You're awfully calm, Thorfinn.

158
00:16:39,420 --> 00:16:42,420
Do you not understand this situation?

159
00:16:44,100 --> 00:16:47,960
We used up the soil's fertility,
but we'll have no harvest.

160
00:16:48,890 --> 00:16:51,920
We'll have to borrow seeds
for the next planting, too.

161
00:16:52,550 --> 00:16:57,560
But more than that, they... they...

162
00:16:58,250 --> 00:17:02,810
They should know the difficulty
and joy of growing wheat.

163
00:17:03,980 --> 00:17:06,280
They're farmers, too!

164
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:11,610
How could they do this?

165
00:17:12,070 --> 00:17:14,030
You should be angry, Thorfinn.

166
00:17:14,030 --> 00:17:17,580
Our wheat has been ruined!

167
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:24,560
I...

168
00:17:25,800 --> 00:17:33,460
Until now, I've been someone
who took and destroyed.

169
00:17:34,950 --> 00:17:41,980
Unlike you, I have no right
to be angry at the retainers.

170
00:17:43,390 --> 00:17:47,780
If you want to kill the retainers,

171
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:53,620
then I deserve to die by your hand
a hundred times over, too.

172
00:18:04,370 --> 00:18:10,980
First, let's calm down. Please, Einar.

173
00:18:18,340 --> 00:18:20,020
I see...

174
00:18:20,020 --> 00:18:23,530
This certainly is awful.

175
00:18:24,020 --> 00:18:28,120
Neither of you saw it happen?

176
00:18:28,670 --> 00:18:29,480
No.

177
00:18:30,030 --> 00:18:34,330
Leave this field the way it is until
I'm finished with my investigation.

178
00:18:34,330 --> 00:18:39,040
They may have left some clues behind.

179
00:18:39,630 --> 00:18:42,910
So, do you have any idea
who might have done it?

180
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:47,320
The retainers.

181
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:50,050
I see...

182
00:18:50,050 --> 00:18:54,110
All right. I'll report
all of this to the master.

183
00:18:54,110 --> 00:18:55,910
Leave the rest to me.

184
00:18:59,180 --> 00:19:04,190
I suffered a lot as a slave, too.

185
00:19:04,730 --> 00:19:12,080
I wondered why my bullies would do something
that didn't benefit them in any way.

186
00:19:13,410 --> 00:19:16,890
People who love to discriminate
can be found everywhere,

187
00:19:16,890 --> 00:19:19,330
but not everyone is like that.

188
00:19:19,990 --> 00:19:22,700
Don't lose hope, you two.

189
00:19:41,320 --> 00:19:42,750
Apparently...

190
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:48,880
the master has really
taken a liking to Arnheid.

191
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:58,120
She doesn't have a deal like ours that
allows her to earn her freedom by working.

192
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:05,200
It seems like she's given up
on ever being free again.

193
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:10,510
Even if they like you,
you become bound to them.

194
00:20:10,510 --> 00:20:13,460
If they hate you, this is how they treat you.

195
00:20:15,620 --> 00:20:20,880
What kind of lives are we living?

196
00:20:31,070 --> 00:20:34,550
That was more work than
I expected. I'm exhausted.

197
00:20:34,550 --> 00:20:37,130
What are you talking about?
You were just watching.

198
00:20:37,130 --> 00:20:37,690
Yeah.

199
00:20:37,690 --> 00:20:39,960
Let's go another way, Einar.

200
00:20:41,820 --> 00:20:44,250
Don't, Einar.

201
00:20:44,250 --> 00:20:47,000
There's no reason for us to sneak around.

202
00:20:49,860 --> 00:20:52,840
Well, speak of the devil.

203
00:20:57,430 --> 00:21:01,010
What's wrong? Why the long faces?

204
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:05,640
Restrain yourself, Einar.
Don't listen to them.

205
00:21:13,050 --> 00:21:16,400
What's your problem? Move.

206
00:21:17,140 --> 00:21:21,160
You're the one who ravaged
our farm, aren't you?

207
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:23,320
What? Farm?

208
00:21:24,020 --> 00:21:26,910
I have no idea what you're talking about.

209
00:21:29,790 --> 00:21:31,010
Einar!

210
00:21:31,010 --> 00:21:35,590
I see, I see. So your farm was ravaged.

211
00:21:35,590 --> 00:21:37,670
I'm sorry to hear that.

212
00:21:38,030 --> 00:21:40,880
But don't let it get you down.

213
00:21:44,040 --> 00:21:46,720
It was wheat grown by slaves.

214
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:50,730
It would've been too putrid
for anyone to eat.

215
00:22:20,410 --> 00:22:22,040
Crap...

216
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:29,310
His jaw looks broken.

217
00:22:32,020 --> 00:22:34,060
What a punch!

218
00:22:34,060 --> 00:22:36,210
You brat!

219
00:22:36,210 --> 00:22:39,400
How dare you, slave! I'll kill you!

220
00:22:42,450 --> 00:22:45,430
Slave this, slave that... Shut up already!

221
00:22:45,430 --> 00:22:47,700
Quit crying and come at me.

222
00:22:47,700 --> 00:22:50,200
Y-You idiot, don't—

223
00:22:51,990 --> 00:22:52,710
Thorfinn.

224
00:22:52,710 --> 00:22:54,040
Are you okay?

225
00:22:55,720 --> 00:22:57,870
Let go, damn it.

226
00:23:03,550 --> 00:23:04,590
Damn you!

227
00:23:04,590 --> 00:23:06,550
D-Don't...

228
00:23:13,440 --> 00:23:15,440
H-Huh?

229
00:23:16,030 --> 00:23:18,580
What are you...

230
00:23:32,160 --> 00:23:35,420
F-Father?

231
00:23:37,540 --> 00:23:41,420
He's telling me something...

232
00:23:44,440 --> 00:23:45,350
It's no use.

233
00:23:46,940 --> 00:23:49,930
I'm... falling...

234
00:25:36,450 --> 00:25:40,000
Oath

235
00:25:37,950 --> 00:25:39,060
"Oath."
